  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 keeps the 5% benchmark and numeric per-model results for purchasers, but removes any sales stop, so exceedance triggers only review and corrective action. S5 keeps the 8/100k trigger but makes recall discretionary and open-ended via corrective action, and S3 contains no retrofit obligation for installed units, with a 24-month start for new models. S1 and S4 land within acceptable ranges: serious incidents reported within 24 hours, and built-in suppression required from 36 months."
